**Summary of what was created:**

**New file**: `Game Design Document/Gameplay Rules/Battle Rules.md`

This document formalizes the complete Battle flow:

- **100.1–100.2** — Battle definition and the four-Stage sequence
- **110** — **Planning Stage**: Battleforce composition, Transports, Reserves, Vanguard designation, Faction Relationship reveal
- **120** — **Deployment Stage**: Deployment Zones (200x100 battlefield, 20-deep zones), simultaneous Vanguard + main deployment, Pre-Engagement Moves
- **130–134** — **Engagement Stage** with the true simultaneous turn system:
  - **Rally Phase** — Morale/Endurance recovery, status cleanup, Reserves eligibility
  - **Issue Orders Phase** — 8 Order types (Hold, Advance, Deploy from Reserves, Run, Charge, Dig In, Fall Back, Surge Action) with typed parameters and restrictions
  - **Execute Phase** — snapshot-calculate-apply resolution model ensuring no Player gains order-of-resolution advantage; 3 Reaction types (Reposition, Evade, Return Fire) declared secretly after Order reveal
  - **Resolve Combat Phase** — Melee resolution, Morale tests, destruction processing, Battle End check
- **140** — **Consolidation Stage**: Victor determination, scoring, casualty processing, battlefield cleanup
- **150** — **Battle End Conditions**: Annihilation, Turn Limit, Objective Complete, Mutual Destruction, Concession
- **29 glossary entries** and **implementation notes** with full state requirements for the digital engine

All rules are deterministic, use explicit numerical values, and avoid ambiguous language. Changes left uncommitted for manual review.
